 ## Subtopics
 
-### Projected Tetrahedra (PT)
-A feedforward projection method often used with this sampling approach [S1, unofficial][S2, book]. It projects cells onto the screen and decomposes them into triangles, handling four classes of projections [S1, unofficial][S2, book]. It is chosen when rendering irregular tetrahedral grids with high accuracy is required [S1, unofficial][S2, book]. See [Projected Tetrahedra](1540-projected-tetrahedra.md).
+### [Octree-based Hierarchical Sampling](20804-octree-based-hierarchical-sampling.md)
+Octree-based Hierarchical Sampling is a technique that uses an octree to determine sampling densities for volumetric data, achieving importance sampling through different sampling densities within the intersection spaces of leaf nodes and training data blocks. It sets itself apart from uniform sampling by allocating sample points proportionally to the geometric overlap between the data block and the octree leaves, and from static hierarchical sampling by dynamically adapting to the data structure's local granularity. It is chosen when dynamic adaptation to local data granularity is required over static or uniform approaches. See [Octree-based Hierarchical Sampling](20804-octree-based-hierarchical-sampling.md).
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Allows rendering within a time-critical framework [S1, unofficial][S2, book]. Exact complexity not given in the sources.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Overcomes the need to fix resolution to the smallest cell, reducing storage requirements compared to a uniform high-resolution grid [S2, book]. Exact memory usage not given in the sources.
